{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given an integer array `nums`, return the number of **reverse pairs**: index pairs `i < j` with `nums[i] > 2 · nums[j]`."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/eb4927d5-efdd-4cd7-b4aa-a027f4d30c1e.svg",
      "alt": "Counting across two sorted halves, 1, 2, 3 and 1, 3. For the left value 3, the right values smaller than 3 divided by 2 — just 1 — count: one pair. For 1 and 2 nothing counts. Because both halves are sorted, the pointer into the right half only moves forward as the left value grows.",
      "width": 588,
      "height": 398,
